Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every individual test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_MustHaveItems() { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before/after all tests in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class CustomerApiTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetCustomer_Returns200() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start in-process WireMock
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // tear down WireMock
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseMigration
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // run EF Core migrations
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // drop test database
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Context type |
|-------|-----------|---------------|--------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | instance | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **static** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, in any class) for a *global* cross-cutting hook that fires for every test across the entire run—handy for logging or timing without touching each test class. The `Class` and `Assembly` variants (`[BeforeEvery(Class)]`, etc.) also exist.

All hooks can be `async Task` and optionally accept a `CancellationToken` as a second parameter.
